2026-09-18 (v1.1.0)
==================
* NEW: opt-in OAuth 2.1 enforcement behind ServerConfig.EnforceOAuth21.
  While the flag is false, every existing code path is unchanged.
  When true, the authorization code flow enforces:
  - PKCE required on every authorization request (rfc7636,
    https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/draft-ietf-oauth-v2-1-15);
    invalid_request when missing for any client
  - exact-match redirect URI validation, with the RFC 8252 §7.3
    loopback port exception for 127.0.0.1 and [::1] over http;
    subpath, query, port (non-loopback), and userinfo differences are
    rejected as invalid_request
  - public clients (no secret) authenticate at the token endpoint with
    the client_id request parameter alone, regardless of
    AllowClientSecretInParams; clients with a secret must still present it
  - new validateUriListExact / validateUriExact / loopbackUriVariant
    in urivalidate.go (used only when EnforceOAuth21 is true)
* Out of scope for this release (other 2.1 gaps remain open): implicit
  and password grant removal, iss metadata parameter, DPoP / mTLS sender
  constraint tokens, discovery and dynamic client registration.
* Internal modernization: interface{} -> any, strings.SplitN -> strings.Cut,
  err.(T) -> errors.AsType[T], time.Until for remaining-expires math,
  cmp.Or for description default in response.go, strings.FieldsSeq +
  slices.Collect + slices.Contains in extraScopes, hoist of duplicate
  FirstUri call in authorize.go, and the previously-discarded
  r.ParseForm() errors in info.go and authorize.go are now checked.
  None of these changes break the public API (any is an alias for
  interface{}).
* Full test coverage for the EnforceOAuth21 paths:
  access_test.go, authorize_test.go, urivalidate_test.go.

2026-09-18 (v1.0.3)
==================
* Internal modernization to Go 1.21+ idioms. No public API changes.
  - interface{} -> any across the package
  - slices.Contains replaces manual linear lookups in
    AllowedAuthorizeType.Exists and AllowedAccessType.Exists
  - strings.Cut replaces strings.SplitN + length check in CheckBasicAuth
    and CheckBearerAuth; strings.EqualFold replaces strings.ToLower
  - errors.AsType[UriValidationError] replaces the type assertion in
    urivalidate.go
  - time.Until replaces CreatedAt.Add(...).Sub(now) chains in info.go
  - cmp.Or replaces if/else for description default in response.go
  - strings.FieldsSeq + slices.Collect + slices.Contains replace the
    manual map-based scope membership check in extraScopes
  - hoisted the duplicate FirstUri call in authorize.go
  - r.ParseForm() errors in info.go and authorize.go are now checked

2026-09-17 (v1.0.2)
==================
* Dependency and toolchain upgrades (requires Go 1.26):
  - go 1.24.0 -> 1.26.0
  - dgrijalva/jwt-go -> github.com/golang-jwt/jwt/v5 v5.3.1
  - square/go-jose.v1 -> github.com/go-jose/go-jose/v4 v4.1.5
  - golang.org/x/oauth2 v0.31.0 -> v0.37.0
  - google/uuid v1.0.0 -> v1.6.0
* Lint / vet fixes:
  - removed unreachable code in access.go (handleAssertionRequest)
  - replaced unkeyed struct literals with field names in BasicAuth
    construction in test files
  - ST1005: error strings lowercased (e.g. "empty client secret",
    "client authentication not sent", "parsing error",
    "request must be POST")
  - SA9004: const types tightened to string
  - SA1019: switched from httptest.ResponseRecorder.HeaderMap to
    .Result().Header
  - S1039: removed redundant fmt.Sprintf in deferror.Get()
* Client auth refactor: getClientAuth now uses r.BasicAuth() instead of
  manual header parsing. When the Authorization header is present the
  client secret (password) must not be empty.

2018-07-18 (v1.0.1)
==================
* Per the OAuth2 spec, query strings in redirect URIs must be kept;
  urivalidate.go now preserves the redirect's RawQuery when resolving
  against the base.
* Reworked redirect URI validation: resolve references against the
  base URL and return the resolved URL to the caller, so subpath
  matches return the actual redirected URL rather than the registered
  one.
* Scope separator is a single space (" "), not a comma (","). The
  extraScopes check now splits on space.
* URL-decode the client_id and client_secret in the Authorization
  header (per RFC 6749 §2.3.1).
* Authorize handler reads from form values via r.FormValue instead of
  r.URL.Query, so x-www-form-urlencoded request bodies are accepted.
* Added a Logger interface for server-side logging.

2014-06-25 (v1.0.0)
==================
* BREAKING CHANGES:
	- Storage interface has 2 new methods, Clone and Close, to better support storages
	  that need to clone / close in each connection (mgo)
	- Client was changed to be an interface instead of an struct. Because of that,
	  the Storage interface also had to change, as interface is already a pointer.

	- HOW TO FIX YOUR CODE:
		+ In your Storage, add a Clone function returning itself, and a do nothing Close.
		+ In your Storage, replace all *osin.Client with osin.Client (remove the pointer reference)
		+ If you used the osin.Client struct directly in your code, change it to osin.DefaultClient,
		  which is a struct with the same fields that implements the interface.
		+ Change all accesses using osin.Client to use the methods instead of the fields directly.
		+ You MUST defer Response.Close in all your http handlers, otherwise some
		  Storages may not clean correctly.

				resp := server.NewResponse()
				defer resp.Close()